From 8b7f5ae54a7d98e8cd732b51a18fbe3223cd2bd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?utf-8?q?J=C3=B8rgen=20H=2E=20Fjeld?= <jorgen@veridit.no>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:17:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] hooks: commit-msg calls hug's Model: <id>/<effort> gate (hug
 jr55s8)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

.githooks/commit-msg now hands the message to hug's gate
(<git-common-dir>/hooks/hug-commit-msg, written by hug task install
commit-msg): exactly one trailer, Model: <model-id>/<effort> or
Model: human, the effort checked against the model's levels in hug.toml
[models] on hug/tasks. Without the gate installed it refuses, with
fix: hug task install commit-msg.

Removed: the Co-Authored-By check and .githooks/known-models.txt (the
roster moves to hug.toml [models]: hug task models add ID LEVEL...), and
SEID_ALLOW_NO_COAUTHOR (bypass: git commit --no-verify). Exemptions are
unchanged: merges, cherry-picks, reverts, rebases, fixup!/squash!/amend!.

compiler/test/infra/test_commit_msg_attribution_guard.sh checks the new
hook: 17 checks, all passing here; on the old hook 7 fail (the
Model: and gate checks) and the 10 exemption checks pass, as before.
TOOLING.md and the two skills name the new trailer.

Ruling: Jørgen 2026-11-17, one trailer line Model: <model-id>/<effort>.

Model: claude-opus-5-5/high
